[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mollama_kimi-k2.6_cloud-bug-fix-trial-2[0m[0m
Fixed. Two surgical changes, one per root cause.

**Root cause 1 — Duplicate processing** (`job_queue.py:26`):
`dequeue()` had `await asyncio.sleep(0.01)` *between* the `if job["status"] == "pending"` check and `job["status"] = "processing"`. In asyncio's cooperative multitasking, that yield allowed every worker to pass the check on the same job before any of them updated the status, so all 5 workers picked up the same job. I moved the status update before the `await` so the check-and-set is atomic.

**Root cause 2 — Vanishing failures** (`worker.py:19-20`):
The worker caught exceptions and printed them but never called `queue.fail()`. The job stayed in `"processing"` forever, so it never retried and never showed up as failed. I added `queue.fail(job["id"], str(e))` in the except block so retries and final failure state work as designed.

After the fix, `main.py` produces the expected counts: `Done: 10`, `Failed: 2`, `Stuck: 0`.
